    <h2>Step-by-Step Guide: How to Batch Convert Images Online</h2>
    <p>
      Converting single photos or bulk collections on RemoveSynth is fast and intuitive across both desktop and mobile devices:
    </p>
    <ol class="steps">
      <li>
        <strong>Drag and Drop Your Images:</strong> Drop up to 30 files into the upload zone above. You can mix and match different formats (e.g., dropping 5 HEIC files, 10 PNGs, and 3 WebP images simultaneously).
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Select Your Target Output Format:</strong> Choose whether you want JPG (maximum universal compatibility), PNG (lossless precision and transparency), WebP (modern web compression), or AVIF (ultra-compact delivery).
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Adjust Quality and Compression Settings:</strong> For lossy output formats, fine-tune the quality slider. We recommend a quality factor of 90 to 92 for optimal fidelity-to-filesize balance.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Instant Parallel Processing:</strong> Dedicated client-side Web Workers process your files simultaneously using multi-core browser threading without freezing your interface.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Download Converted Files:</strong> Download images individually or click Download All as ZIP to receive a consolidated archive containing your entire converted batch.
      </li>
    </ol>

